## For any module install file 
1. Check if this module already exist and installed
2. Check if all the plugins / themes / addons are also installed
3. Check if an existing configuration exist and make a backup in the backup directory of the project
4. Install what is missing from the list
5. Apply the configuration with stow. DO NOT COPY ANY FILE

### Module Install Script Standard Format
Each module's install.sh should follow this structure:

```bash
#!/bin/bash

# Exit on any error
set -e

# Script directory and module info
SCRIPT_DIR="$( cd "$( dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]}" )" && pwd )"
BACKUP_DIR="$SCRIPT_DIR/../backup"
MODULE_NAME="module_name"

# Catppuccin Mocha color scheme
# Base colors
BASE="\033[0m"
TEXT="\033[38;2;205;214;244m"      # Text
SUBTEXT="\033[38;2;166;173;200m"   # Subtext
OVERLAY="\033[38;2;108;112;134m"   # Overlay
SURFACE="\033[38;2;49;50;68m"      # Surface
BASE_COLOR="\033[38;2;30;30;46m"   # Base
MANTLE="\033[38;2;24;24;37m"       # Mantle
CRUST="\033[38;2;17;17;27m"        # Crust

# Accent colors
RED="\033[38;2;243;139;168m"       # Red
GREEN="\033[38;2;166;227;161m"     # Green
YELLOW="\033[38;2;249;226;175m"    # Yellow
BLUE="\033[38;2;137;180;250m"      # Blue
PINK="\033[38;2;245;194;231m"      # Pink
MAUVE="\033[38;2;203;166;247m"     # Mauve
TEAL="\033[38;2;148;226;213m"      # Teal

# Print functions
print_status() {
    echo -e "${BLUE}[i]${BASE} $1"
}

print_success() {
    echo -e "${GREEN}[✓]${BASE} $1"
}

print_error() {
    echo -e "${RED}[✗]${BASE} $1"
}

print_warning() {
    echo -e "${YELLOW}[!]${BASE} $1"
}

print_header() {
    echo -e "\n${MAUVE}=== $1 ===${BASE}\n"
}

# Print module header
print_header "Installing $MODULE_NAME configuration"

# Module-specific installation steps here
# ...

# Use stow to create symlinks
print_status "Installing $MODULE_NAME configuration..."
if ! stow -t "$HOME" .; then
    print_error "Failed to install $MODULE_NAME configuration"
    exit 1
fi

print_success "$MODULE_NAME configuration installed successfully!"
```

Key requirements for module install scripts:
1. Must use the Catppuccin Mocha color scheme
2. Must include proper error handling
3. Must create backups before modifying existing configurations
4. Must use stow for configuration management
5. Must provide clear status messages
6. Must exit with appropriate error codes
7. Must use consistent naming and formatting

