# Docker

## Overview
The Docker setup provides a clean, isolated environment for testing the dotfiles configuration. It uses Ubuntu 24.04 LTS as the base image to match the target environment.

## Directory Structure
```
.
├── Dockerfile           # Container definition
├── docker-compose.yml  # Container orchestration
└── entrypoint.sh       # Container initialization
```

## Dockerfile Requirements
```dockerfile
# Use Ubuntu 24.04 LTS as base
FROM ubuntu:24.04

# Set environment variables
ENV DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
ENV HOME=/root

# Install essential packages
RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y \
    git \
    stow \
    zsh \
    curl \
    wget \
    sudo \
    && rm -rf /var/lib/apt/lists/*

# Set up working directory
WORKDIR /root/dotfiles

# Copy dotfiles
COPY . .

# Make scripts executable
RUN chmod +x install.sh test-all.sh entrypoint.sh

# Set entrypoint
ENTRYPOINT ["/root/dotfiles/entrypoint.sh"]
```

## docker-compose.yml Requirements
```yaml
version: '3.8'

services:
  dotfiles:
    build:
      context: .
      dockerfile: Dockerfile
    volumes:
      - .:/root/dotfiles
    environment:
      - TERM=xterm-256color
    tty: true
    stdin_open: true
```

## entrypoint.sh Requirements
```bash
#!/bin/bash

# Exit on error
set -e

# Print functions (using Catppuccin Mocha colors)
print_header() {
    echo -e "\n\033[38;2;203;166;247m=== $1 ===\033[0m\n"
}

print_success() {
    echo -e "\033[38;2;166;227;161m[✓] $1\033[0m"
}

print_error() {
    echo -e "\033[38;2;243;139;168m[✗] $1\033[0m"
}

# Main execution
print_header "Starting dotfiles installation in Docker"

# Run installation
if [ -f "/root/dotfiles/install.sh" ]; then
    print_success "Running installation script"
    /root/dotfiles/install.sh --all
else
    print_error "Installation script not found"
    exit 1
fi

# Run tests
if [ -f "/root/dotfiles/test-all.sh" ]; then
    print_success "Running test suite"
    /root/dotfiles/test-all.sh
else
    print_error "Test script not found"
    exit 1
fi

# Keep container running for inspection
print_success "Installation and tests completed"
print_success "Container will remain running for inspection"
print_success "Use 'docker exec -it <container_id> zsh' to access the container"

# Keep container running
tail -f /dev/null
```

